    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105062" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρί-μορφος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>three-formed,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑκάτη τριοδῖτι, τρίμορφε, τριπρόσωπε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chariclid.
					1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				1176
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				34
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν τ. θεὸν ἔτι κυόμενον ἐν τῷ
					ᾠῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					60
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαῖρε πάτερ κόσμου, χαῖρε τρίμορφε
					θεός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>CIG</u>
					4971
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Egypt</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				6128
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> pl., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρεῖς, Μοῖραι τ.</span>
			 the <i>three</i> fates, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				516
			</span></i>.</div>
